kouts_heartbeat_directory(tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmp5bs3eqqo/diff.patch:3143:+    \"\"\"write_invocation_marker's own `events` field, from `attavo drive`\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmp5bs3eqqo/diff.patch:3144:+    itself (#289): the marker is committed and pushed from a detached\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmp5bs3eqqo/diff.patch:3147:+    checkout reading this marker later would look for the heartbeat in a\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmp5bs3eqqo/diff.patch:3148:+    directory removed the moment the marker's own push returned.\"\"\"\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmp5bs3eqqo/diff.patch:3151:+    marker = json.loads((records_dir(root) / \"build-01.started\").read_text())\n/var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmp5bs3eqqo/diff.patch:3152:+    assert marker[\"events\"] == str(git_dir(root) / \"attavo\"), marker\nattest/specs/289/criteria/a-second-checkout-reads-the-holders-heartbeat-where-its-marker-says.sh:17:from attavo.doctor import write_invocation_marker\nattest/specs/289/criteria/a-second-checkout-reads-the-holders-heartbeat-where-its-marker-says.sh:21:marker = write_invocation_marker(root, records, \"build\", 1)\nattest/specs/289/criteria/a-second-checkout-reads-the-holders-heartbeat-where-its-marker-says.sh:22:info = json.loads(marker.read_text())\nattest/specs/289/criteria/a-second-checkout-reads-the-holders-heartbeat-where-its-marker-says.sh:29:assert read_invocation(root, 600, marker, info).cls == \"running\", \"a fresh heartbeat where the marker says\"\nattest/specs/289/criteria/a-second-checkout-reads-the-holders-heartbeat-where-its-marker-says.sh:31:assert read_invocation(root, 600, marker, info).cls == \"running\", \"no first beat yet, younger than the bound\"\nattest/specs/289/criteria/a-second-checkout-reads-the-holders-heartbeat-where-its-marker-says.sh:33:assert read_invocation(root, 600, marker, old).cls == \"died\", \"no heartbeat, older than the bound\"\nattest/specs/289/criteria/a-second-checkout-reads-the-holders-heartbeat-where-its-marker-says.sh:35:assert read_invocation(root, 600, marker, legacy).cls == \"died\", \"a marker naming no directory reads as before\"\nattest/specs/289/criteria/a-second-checkout-reads-the-holders-heartbeat-where-its-marker-says.sh:38:for t in test_a_second_checkout_on_this_host_reads_the_first_ones_worker_as_running test_the_holders_heartbeat_is_read_where_its_marker_says test_the_marker_a_pass_writes_names_its_checkouts_heartbeat_directory\nattest/specs/289/spec.md:6:`test_two_passes_at_once_start_one_worker_and_the_loser_says_so` fails intermittently. It failed in full runs on `d4c0bc1` and `5df6926`, and it knocked #273 out of the merge queue once. When it fails, both passes print \"Build started\". It was filed as #289, \"the pass lock admits two workers under load\", and it is not a lock problem.\nattest/specs/289/spec.md:8:The lease is sound. Only one marker push can land. The defect is in how the losing pass reads the winner's live invocation, and the specimen is the test itself. Two clones of one tenant sit on one host. Pass A pushes `build-01.started` and starts its worker. Its worker writes its heartbeat under A's git dir: `stage_events_dir` is `<git-dir>/attavo`, per checkout, and per linked worktree too. Pass B then fetches and fast-forwards, sees A's marker with no record, and asks `read_invocation` whether it is running. The marker's `host` is B's own host, and B looks for the heartbeat in its own git dir, finds none, and reads \"died\". So it recovers, or starts a second attempt.\nattest/specs/289/spec.md:14:This item makes the marker say where its holder beats, and every reader read there.\nattest/specs/289/spec.md:16:- `write_invocation_marker` adds `events`, the absolute directory the holder's heartbeat will be written in. The pass writes the marker from a detached worktree, so `_start_stage` passes the checkout's own `stage_events_dir(root)`, never the worktree's.\nattest/specs/289/spec.md:18:  - a marker from this host that names a directory is read in that directory;\nattest/specs/289/spec.md:19:  - a marker from this host written before markers named one keeps this checkout's own directory;\nattest/specs/289/spec.md:20:  - a marker from another host returns None, since no file here holds its heartbeat.\nattest/specs/289/spec.md:22:- When a marker from this host names a directory that holds no heartbeat yet, the invocation is treated like one from another host: running while the marker is younger than the stall bound, died after. That covers another checkout's worker that has not reached its first beat. A stale heartbeat is still died, and the stall bound still decides hung, never died.\nattest/specs/289/spec.md:23:- A marker without `events` keeps the old reading exactly, so the markers already in the records read as they did.\nattest/specs/289/spec.md:27:- the race made deterministic: a second clone's pass after the first has started reads running, starts nothing, and no second invocation is pushed;\nattest/specs/289/spec.md:28:- the heartbeat read where the marker says: fresh there, absent while young, absent when old, and a legacy marker;\nattest/specs/289/spec.md:29:- the marker a pass writes names its checkout's directory.\nattest/specs/289/spec.md:43:- a-second-checkout-reads-the-holders-heartbeat-where-its-marker-says.sh: on the fixture tenant, with no test runner, `write_invocation_marker` writes `events` as the checkout's own `<git-dir>/attavo`; `read_invocation` reads a marker from this host naming another directory as running with a fresh heartbeat there, running with none yet while younger than the stall bound, and died when older; a marker naming no directory reads died as before; and `tests/test_pass.py` carries the three tests named\nattest/specs/289/stub/attavo/doctor.py:167:INVOCATION_MARKER_SUFFIX = \".started\"\nattest/specs/289/stub/attavo/doctor.py:1